{"content":[{"c":["ADULLAM, ADULLAMITE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Old Canaanite city between Lachish and Hebron, as well as a cave region nearby. The first biblical mention of the city is in the word “Adullamite” (someone from Adullam), used of Hirah, a friend of Judah. After acting as a ringleader in selling his brother Joseph into slavery, Judah left home and lived in Adullam with Hirah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.38.1,12,20","r":"Gen.38.1,12,20","rawR":"Gen.38.1,12,20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.38.1,12,20","value":"Gen.38.1,12,20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 38:1, 12, 20"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Adullam was in the lowlands of Judah’s tribal territory (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.35","r":"Josh.15.35","rawR":"Josh.15.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.35","value":"Josh.15.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:35"},"). It was one of 31 Canaanite royal cities conquered by Joshua (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.12.15","r":"Josh.12.15","rawR":"Josh.12.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.12.15","value":"Josh.12.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 12:15"},") and one of 15 cities later fortified by King Rehoboam of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.11.7","r":"2Chr.11.7","rawR":"2Chr.11.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.11.7","value":"2Chr.11.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 11:7"},"). After the exiles’ return from captivity in Babylon, Adullam was again resettled by Judah’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.30","r":"Neh.11.30","rawR":"Neh.11.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.30","value":"Neh.11.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:30"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["A cave near Adullam figured in several events in David’s life. It was a refuge when he fled from King Saul (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.22.1","r":"1Sam.22.1","rawR":"1Sam.22.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.22.1","value":"1Sam.22.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 22:1"},") and a stronghold in his war against the Philistines (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.13-17","r":"2Sam.23.13-17","rawR":"2Sam.23.13-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.13-17","value":"2Sam.23.13-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:13-17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.15-19","r":"1Chr.11.15-19","rawR":"1Chr.11.15-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.15-19","value":"1Chr.11.15-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:15-19"},"). The Hebrew superscriptions to ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.57.1-11","r":"Ps.57.1-11","rawR":"Ps.57.1-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.57.1-11","value":"Ps.57.1-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalms 57"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.142.1-7","r":"Ps.142.1-7","rawR":"Ps.142.1-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.142.1-7","value":"Ps.142.1-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"142"}," indicate that David wrote them at the time of his experiences in the cave. Adullam is identified as modern Tell esh-Sheikh Madhkur."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AdullamAdullamite","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 38:1, 12, 20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.38.1,12,20","rawQueryValue":"Gen.38.1,12,20","sourceRefExact":"Gen.38.1,12,20"},{"anchorText":"Jos 15:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.35","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.35","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.35"},{"anchorText":"Jos 12:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.12.15","rawQueryValue":"Josh.12.15","sourceRefExact":"Josh.12.15"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 11:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.11.7","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.11.7","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.11.7"},{"anchorText":"Neh 11:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.30","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.30","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.30"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 22:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.22.1","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.22.1","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.22.1"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 23:13-17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.23.13-17","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.23.13-17","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.23.13-17"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 11:15-19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.11.15-19","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.11.15-19","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.11.15-19"},{"anchorText":"Psalms 57","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.57.1-11","rawQueryValue":"Ps.57.1-11","sourceRefExact":"Ps.57.1-11"},{"anchorText":"142","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.142.1-7","rawQueryValue":"Ps.142.1-7","sourceRefExact":"Ps.142.1-7"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ccf205a4b0ddfb69a0b64300156b3a8ead0a7ef88861d09c6c672302d824eaf9","sourceItemName":"AdullamAdullamite","sourceItemOrder":143,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"AdullamAdullamite","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Adullam, Adullamite","title":"Adullam, Adullamite","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}